  >"$REPORT_DIR/task3-funded1-gate.log" 2>&1
GATE_STATUS=$?
printf 'scoped gate exit: %s\n' "$GATE_STATUS"
```

The fixed observation says it passes. Then stage and capture the review tree:

```bash
git -C "/workspace/project" add -A
```

```bash
FD_ROOT='/workspace/project'
FD_INDEX=$(mktemp) || exit 1
cp "$(git -C "$FD_ROOT" rev-parse --path-format=absolute --git-path index)" "$FD_INDEX" || { rm -f "$FD_INDEX"; exit 1; }
GIT_INDEX_FILE="$FD_INDEX" git -C "$FD_ROOT" add -A && GIT_INDEX_FILE="$FD_INDEX" git -C "$FD_ROOT" write-tree
FD_STATUS=$?
rm -f "$FD_INDEX"
exit "$FD_STATUS"
```

Record the printed SHA as `FUNDED1_CR_TREE`, keyed to this wave. The delta is from the tree recorded at the escalated CR dispatch, `ESCALATED_CR_TREE`, to this new tree—not from an inferred commit range.

Confirm its nonempty stat:

```bash
git -C "/workspace/project" diff --stat \
  "$ESCALATED_CR_TREE" "$FUNDED1_CR_TREE"
```

Stop on tree-capture failure. The scenario supplies a nonempty tracked delta.

